# Future feature card formatting

Future-feature **body** and **execution notes** are plain text. The UI enhances each grid card via `src/lib/futureFeatureFormat.tsx`. Write content so those rules fire cleanly.

## Split into cards

- Blank line between paragraphs → separate cards (preferred)
- If there are no blank lines, each non-empty line becomes its own card

## Auto bold (short phrases)

Short title-like lines render **bold**:

- ≤ 6 words and ≤ 48 characters, or
- Ends with `:` and ≤ 8 words / ≤ 60 characters

Prefer short section labels (`Desired behavior:`, `UX notes`) on their own line. Do not rely on markdown `**bold**`.

## Auto dots (bullets)

Start a line with `-` or `*` (also `•` / en/em dash). The marker becomes a round dot; the rest of the line is the content.

```
- Keep separate run records
* Surface failures clearly
```

## Cool numbering

Start a line with `1)`, `1.`, `1-`, or `1:` (any integer). The number renders large and bold on its own line; the phrase sits on the next line (and auto-bolds when short).

```
1) Cron / schedule
2) Manual runs
```

Put bullet details on following lines under that numbered heading (same card or the next card after a blank line).

## Example shape

```
Keep processes separate — that stay intentional.

Desired behavior:

1) Cron / schedule
- Run HIS right after successful TAS
- Skip HIS when disabled

2) Manual runs
- Manual HIS always runs TAS first
```
